.TH DCC-GUI 1 2026-11-28 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc-gui \- desktop application of Dudes Control Center
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcc-gui
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.RB [ \-\-minimized | \-\-show ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcc-gui
is the GTK3 front end for the fan, CPU and keyboard daemons.
It runs as the desktop user and talks to the daemons over their sockets, so
the user must be a member of the group
.BR dudes-control-center .
Only one instance runs at a time; a second start opens the running one's
window and exits (also with
.BR \-\-minimized ,
which only decides how a fresh start begins).
Closing the window hides it; the application keeps running in the tray until
.B Exit
is chosen in the tray menu.
.SS Tabs
.TP
.B Status
Temperatures (CPU, GPU, SSDs), fan speeds with the manual speed control,
the clocks, load and video memory of an NVIDIA, AMD or Intel GPU, as far as
the driver offers them (a powered-down GPU is not woken up), power (CPU package with its sustained limit, GPU, the laptop on
battery), the battery, the active profiles, CPU frequencies per core, and
the system: model, BIOS, processor, graphics, memory, drives, operating
system and kernel.
.TP
.B Fan
Fan curves (temperature to fan speed) with a graph, fixed speeds in 10\~% steps
and automatic mode.
.TP
.B CPU
The processor (name; P- and E-cores on hybrid Intel CPUs), governor,
the firmware power profile a frequency profile sets (on laptops that offer
one), per-core frequency profiles and the hard frequency limit.
.TP
.B Keyboard
Keyboard profiles with a base color and named zones, edited on a picture of
the keyboard (click or drag to select keys), effects (Breathing, Rainbow,
Wave) per zone or for the base color, brightness, on/off and the LED wizard
that maps keys to LEDs.
.TP
.B Settings
Four pages, chosen in a list on the left; the page shown last comes back.
General: language, appearance (system, dark, light), start minimized to the
tray or with the window open, refresh interval of the live values (1, 2, 3,
5 or 10 seconds).
Components: switching the fan, CPU or keyboard part on or off.
Hardware: the battery charge limit and the keyboard layout.
Other laptops: generic fan control and direct EC access for laptops without
the Clevo interface, marked in the list while direct EC access is on.
Switching components and the two options for other laptops asks for the
administrator password (see
.BR dcc-component (8)).
.TP
.B Logs
The daemon and GUI logs.
.TP
.B Help
The README, the changelog and the license (from
.IR /usr/share/doc/dudes-control-center ),
formatted, with clickable links and a search field.
.TP
.B About
Version and credits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Also write routine messages to the GUI log (every refresh and daemon reply);
by default it records events only.
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start as an icon in the system tray.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Start with the window open.
.PP
Without either option the setting
.I Start minimized to tray
in the Settings tab decides (on by default). Switching it writes
.B \-\-minimized
into the Exec line of the application menu entry (a copy in
.IR ~/.local/share/applications )
and of the user's startup applications in
.I ~/.config/autostart
that start
.BR dcc-gui ,
or removes it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after
.B Exit
in the tray menu, and when another instance is already running.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANGUAGE ", " LANG
Used for the interface language when the Settings tab is set to the system
language.
Available: English, German, Spanish, Japanese, Korean, British English.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dudes-control-center/config.json
GUI settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dudes-control-center/profiles.json
Fan, CPU and keyboard profiles (shared with the daemons).
.TP
.I ~/.config/dudes-control-center/keyboard_led_mapping_<layout>.csv
LED wizard mapping per keyboard layout.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/dudes-control-center/logs/GUI.log
GUI log.
.TP
.IR /usr/share/doc/dudes-control-center/ { README.md , CHANGELOG.md , LICENSE }
Shown in the Help tab.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-fan-cli (1),
.BR dcc-cpu-cli (1),
.BR dcc-kbd-cli (1),
.BR dcc-component (8)
